//============================================================================
//  Pin constraints for the Sipeed TANG_SDRAM module (40-pin header).
//
//  *** PIN LOCATIONS ARE NOT FILLED IN YET. ***
//
//  The signal set below is complete and matches tang/gametank_tang.sv, but the
//  FPGA pin for each one depends on the Tang Mega 138K Pro Dock's 40-pin
//  header wiring, which is not published in the Sipeed example projects or the
//  wiki. Fill them from the dock schematic (Sipeed's board documentation
//  package) before building with the `sdram` option — tang/syn.tcl refuses to
//  run without at least one IO_LOC here, precisely so a half-configured build
//  cannot be flashed onto a board with a module attached.
//
//  Two warnings when reading the schematic:
//    - The module is NOT pin-compatible with a MiSTer SDRAM v3.0 board; pins
//      29 and 30 of the 40P connector differ.
//    - The module carries two 16-bit chips. This controller drives one; if the
//      second shares address/command and differs only by chip select, tie its
//      CS inactive or extend tang/sdram.sv.
//
//  Signals to place (all LVCMOS33, 8 mA, no pull):
//    sdram_clk, sdram_cke, sdram_cs_n, sdram_ras_n, sdram_cas_n, sdram_we_n
//    sdram_ba[1:0], sdram_a[12:0], sdram_dqm[1:0], sdram_dq[15:0]
//
//  Template — uncomment and complete:
//
//  IO_LOC "sdram_clk" <pin>;
//  IO_PORT "sdram_clk" IO_TYPE=LVCMOS33 PULL_MODE=NONE DRIVE=8 BANK_VCCIO=3.3;
//  IO_LOC "sdram_dq[0]" <pin>;
//  IO_PORT "sdram_dq[0]" IO_TYPE=LVCMOS33 PULL_MODE=NONE DRIVE=8 BANK_VCCIO=3.3;
//  ... and so on for every signal above.
//============================================================================
